BREACHWATCH

Status: 🟠 Confirmed breach / published data / scope reconciliation continuing

What is confirmed

Charter experienced a cybersecurity incident.
Charter said business-customer sales tools were affected.
Charter denied that sensitive PI or CPNI was released.
A dataset attributed to Charter was subsequently published.
HIBP indexed approximately 4.9 million unique email addresses from the breach dataset.

What is claimed

ShinyHunters carried out the attack.
Initial compromise occurred April 1.
Voice phishing targeted a Charter employee.
A Microsoft Entra identity was compromised.
The identity provided access to Charter's Salesforce environment.
40–42 million records were obtained.
Some CPNI was present in the stolen material.

What InfinityGrid is watching

Charter's final regulatory notification
definitive affected-person count
reconciliation between 4.9M unique emails and 40M+ claimed records
whether CPNI is independently confirmed
precise Entra compromise mechanism
whether MFA enrollment/reset was manipulated
whether an attacker-controlled MFA device was registered
whether session tokens were stolen
Salesforce permissions of the compromised user
export method used
Bulk API involvement
data-retention scope
whether business and consumer environments shared CRM data
lawsuits and regulator findings
